From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:01:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 08/40] Metal diamond engine: lumped RLC elements on the GPU
 (snapshot cg20)

The lumped RLC extension runs per tile in the engine's Apply order, mixed
with the Mur faces (same priority): one state record per element (Il,
Vd[n-1], Vd[n-2], J[n-1], J[n-2]) instead of the CPU's rotating arrays,
the inductor current, node voltage and J with clang's contraction of the
CPU expressions, all reads before all writes (one thread in element order
when two elements share a cell). Per-tile element lists as for the
excitation. The patch tutorial and patch x5 (Mur + lumped port + nf2ff)
now run on the GPU: port probes, S11 and nf2ff dumps bit-identical to the
multithreaded engine with OPENEMS_FTZ=1; patch x5 2719 MC/s vs 1342 on the
CPU under the same load. emsKit diamond_check.sh: 24/24 identical (new
case: parallel RLC, series RLC, series LC).

Generated-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
